figdown 0.1 bitfield
# `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION`: `present=` is a TRI-STATE, parallel to `class ""` (`CLASS-EMPTY-MEANING`)
# and to the label tri-state (`EMPTY-LABEL-STATE`).
#   key ABSENT    no presence claim — NOT an assertion that the field is
#                 always present
#   present=""    conditional; condition NOT stated (the author claimed
#                 nothing, and an agent MUST NOT invent one)
#   present="…"   conditional; condition stated, as opaque authored prose
# The value is syntactically mandatory: there is no bare form.
bitfield hdr "Presence tri-state" word=32 numbering=msb0
field "Always" 8
field "Maybe" 8 present=""
field "IfC" 16 present="C = 1"
field "Compact and line-wide" 32 present="the K bit is set" description="the key is available on the compact form too, where it is LINE-wide"
field a:8,b:8,c:8,d:8 present="S = 1"
